ening \`Layout\`; widths are positive pixels, and an empty slot leaves that column automatic.\\n- Images use ordinary Markdown image syntax and an existing project-relative asset path, as in \`![Realm map](assets/realm-map.png)\`. Do not emit internal \`asset:\` identifiers or signed URLs.\\n- A picture is shown at its own size unless it carries a display width. To give it one, use raw HTML \`<img src=\\"assets/realm-map.png\\" alt=\\"Realm map\\" width=\\"240\\" />\`, where the width is whole pixels. Keep Markdown image syntax for every picture that has no width.\\n\\nSpecialized diagram and link references are a deeper tier. When the harness offers one, load it before uncommon formatting; this core card remains authoritative for wire spelling.\\n\\nContext file URI rules: bare file paths resolve as \`manuscript://\` -- the writer's manuscript documents. \`kb://\` is the project knowledge base (durable reference: characters, places, canon). \`unfiled://\` holds project-owned autosaved documents not yet filed into a manuscript or reference location. They can be read, edited and moved like other project documents; naming alone does not file them. \`scratch://\` holds working files for this Work -- plans, notes, intermediate material; never the manuscript. \`scratch://@<slug>/...\` addresses another Work in this project. File and folder names cannot begin with \`@\` in any scheme or at any depth. Switch Works and an unqualified \`scratch://\` path resolves in a different scratch space. Anything meant to outlive this Work belongs in \`kb://\` or the manuscript. \`uploads://\` holds files the writer attached to this Work (same scoping). \`user://\` is the writer's personal files. To read a document, call \`write\` with both \`command: \\"read\\"\` and \`path\`; for example \`write({command: \\"read\\", path: \\"manuscript://chapter.md\\"})\`. Use \`ls\` and \`search\` for discovery. The \`diff\` command is only for this turn's folded edit result and requires a Work in draft write mode, not document reading."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system_update>\\nConversation summary. Earlier turns of this conversation (c1) were compacted into the summary below.\\nContinue from this summary and the messages after it; do not redo finished work.\\n\\nEarlier context.\\n</system_update>"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"old answer"},{"type":"tool_use","toolCallId":"stale-read","toolName":"write","input":{"path":"manuscript://chapter.md","command":"read"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","toolCallId":"stale-read","output":"[Cleared at compaction: manuscript://chapter.md has changed since this read. Read it again before relying on its text.]","isError":false}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","toolCallId":"fresh-read","toolName":"write","input":{"path":"manuscript://chapter.md","command":"read"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","toolCallId":"fresh-read","output":"FRESH-READ TEXT","isError":false}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","toolCallId":"stale-write","toolName":"write","input":{"in":"b41","path":"manuscript://chapter.md","command":"replace"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","toolCallId":"stale-write","output":"[Cleared at compaction: you edited manuscript://chapter.md here (replace); it has changed since. Read it before relying on this edit.]","isError":false}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","toolCallId":"fresh-write","toolName":"write","input":{"in":"b41","find":"FRESH-WRITE TEXT","path":"manuscript://chapter.md","command":"replace","content":"FRESH-WRITE TEXT"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","toolCallId":"fresh-write","output":"FRESH-WRITE TEXT","isError":false}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","toolCallId":"search","toolName":"search","input":{"pattern":"dragon"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","toolCallId":"search","output"